- (used by coordinator when proposing next week's plan)

## Communication style

- **Tone**: {{COMM_TONE}} (1–5; 1 = gentle, 5 = ruthless)
- **Default format**: {{COMM_FORMAT}} (bullets / prose / tables / mixed)

## Protocol mode

*How long-running protocols (WEEKLY_REVIEW, MONTHLY_REVIEW, SEASON_TRANSITION, SEASON_PLANNING) handle their pause-points. See the "HOW THIS PROTOCOL RUNS" header of each protocol in `PROTOCOLS.md`.*

- **PROTOCOL_MODE**: {{PROTOCOL_MODE}}
  - `checkpoints` — mentor pauses at each gate (Signal Brief, Plan Approval, etc.) and waits for your reply before continuing. Safer; recommended while you are calibrating the system.
  - `automated` — mentor runs the whole protocol end-to-end with no pauses, makes its own best-judgement decisions at every gate, and delivers a single final report you can audit and roll back if needed.

You can change this value any time without re-running `init.sh` — protocols re-read this file at the start of each run.

